[{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (8x+1)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (6x^2-3)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (10x^3+9)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (3x+5)(4x^2-1)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"4x^2+x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x^3-3x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac52x^4+9x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(12x^3+20x^2-3x-5)\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=3x^4+\\frac{20}3x^3-\\frac32x^2-5x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac23x+\\dfrac53x^4\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac34x^2-\\dfrac{14}3x^6\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac25x^7-\\dfrac38x^5\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac13x^2+4\\right)\\left(\\dfrac23x^2+6\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac13x^2+\\frac13x^5+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac14x^3-\\frac23x^7+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1{20}x^8-\\frac1{16}x^6+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\left(\\frac29x^4+\\frac{14}3x^2+24\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=\\frac2{45}x^5+\\frac{14}9x^3+24x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=2-2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Sketch the family of solutions that solve this differential equation.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2x-x^2+c.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.36/solutions/assets/s03.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\left(\\dfrac x2-1\\right)\\left(\\dfrac x3+1\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=ax^3+bx^2+cx+d\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b,c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are rational numbers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac16x^2+\\frac16x-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{18}x^3+\\frac1{12}x^2-x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(6,1):1=12+3-6+c\\Rightarrow c=-8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{18}x^3+\\frac1{12}x^2-x-8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given the gradient function is:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=x^{2/3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=6x^{1/5}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=21x^{3/4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=(2x^{1/6}+3)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac35x^{5/3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=5x^{6/5}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=12x^{7/4}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=4x^{1/3}+12x^{1/6}+9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=3x^{4/3}+\\frac{72}7x^{7/6}+9x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (x^3+x^{3/2})\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (5x^{-2}-2x^{2/3})\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (8x^{-3}-4x^{6/5})\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (2x^{-4}-3x^{4/3})^2\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac14x^4+\\frac25x^{5/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-5x^{-1}-\\frac65x^{5/3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-4x^{-2}-\\frac{20}{11}x^{11/5}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(4x^{-8}-12x^{-8/3}+9x^{8/3})\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=-\\frac47x^{-7}+\\frac{36}5x^{-5/3}+\\frac{27}{11}x^{11/3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Find  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int (1-x^{-2})(1-x^{-4})\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(1-x^{-4}-x^{-2}+x^{-6})\\,dx=x+\\frac13x^{-3}+x^{-1}-\\frac15x^{-5}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=40x^{1/3}-4x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=ax^{4/3}+bx^2+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=30x^{4/3}-2x^2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1,-1):-1=30-2+c\\Rightarrow c=-29\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=30x^{4/3}-2x^2-29\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given the gradient function is:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=5-2x^{-4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=6x^{-3}(x-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=x^{1/2}(8x-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=(2x^{3/2}-3)(2x^{-7/2}+7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=5x+\\frac23x^{-3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=6x^{-2}-12x^{-3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-6x^{-1}+6x^{-2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=8x^{3/2}-3x^{1/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{16}5x^{5/2}-2x^{3/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=4x^{-2}+14x^{3/2}-6x^{-7/2}-21\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-4x^{-1}+\\frac{28}5x^{5/2}+\\frac{12}5x^{-5/2}-21x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int 4\\sqrt{x}(x-1)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\sqrt[4]{x}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\sqrt[5]{32x}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\sqrt[4]{81x^{1/4}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(4x^{3/2}-4x^{1/2})\\,dx=\\frac85x^{5/2}-\\frac83x^{3/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int x^{1/4}\\,dx=\\frac45x^{5/4}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int2x^{1/5}\\,dx=\\frac53x^{6/5}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int3x^{1/16}\\,dx=\\frac{48}{17}x^{17/16}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=x^2(7\\sqrt{x}-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=ax^{7/2}-bx^3+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=7x^{5/2}-3x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2x^{7/2}-x^3+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1,-4):-4=2-1+c\\Rightarrow c=-5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2x^{7/2}-x^3-5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given the gradient function is:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac4{x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac6{x^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac9{5x^4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{100}{9x^{10}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=4x^{-2}\\text{ so }y=-4x^{-1}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=6x^{-3}\\text{ so }y=-3x^{-2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac95x^{-4}\\text{ so }y=-\\frac35x^{-3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{100}9x^{-10}\\text{ so }y=-\\frac{100}{81}x^{-9}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac4{3\\sqrt{x}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac6{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac8{\\sqrt[5]{x}}-\\dfrac{100}{\\sqrt[3]{8x}}\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac1{\\sqrt[3]{x}}-\\dfrac3{x\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\frac43x^{-1/2}\\,dx=\\frac83x^{1/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int6x^{-1/3}\\,dx=9x^{2/3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(8x^{-1/5}-50x^{-1/3})\\,dx=10x^{4/5}-75x^{2/3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(x^{-2/3}-6x^{-11/6}+9x^{-3})\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=3x^{1/3}-\\frac{36}5x^{-5/6}-\\frac92x^{-2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac8{\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(16,-8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a(2\\sqrt{x}+b)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=8x^{-1/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=16x^{1/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(16,-8):-8=64+c\\Rightarrow c=-72\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=16x^{1/2}-72\\Rightarrow y=8(2\\sqrt{x}-9)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{750}{x^4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,248)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a\\left(1-\\dfrac1{x^3}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an integer.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=750x^{-4}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-250x^{-3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(5,248):248=-2+c\\Rightarrow c=250\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-250x^{-3}+250\\Rightarrow y=250\\left(1-\\frac1{x^3}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac6{x\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a\\left(\\sqrt b+\\dfrac c{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=6x^{-3/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-12x^{-1/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(8,0):0=-3\\sqrt2+c\\Rightarrow c=3\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-12x^{-1/2}+3\\sqrt2\\Rightarrow y=3\\left(\\sqrt2-\\frac4{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{12}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(27,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a(x^{2/3}+b)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=12x^{-1/3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=18x^{2/3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(27,0):0=162+c\\Rightarrow c=-162\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=18x^{2/3}-162\\Rightarrow y=18(x^{2/3}-9)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac1{x^3\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(1,\\dfrac35\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a-\\dfrac b{cx^2\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x^{-7/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac25x^{-5/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left(1,\\frac35\\right):\\frac35=-\\frac25+c\\Rightarrow c=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac25x^{-5/2}+1\\Rightarrow y=1-\\frac2{5x^{5/2}}\\Rightarrow y=1-\\frac2{5x^2\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q19","number":19,"question":"<p>Find  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac4{x^2\\sqrt{x}}-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x}}{4x^2}\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\left(4x^{-5/2}-\\frac14x^{-3/2}\\right)\\,dx=-\\frac83x^{-3/2}+\\frac12x^{-1/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q20","number":20,"question":"<p>Find  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac6{5x^3\\sqrt{x}}-\\dfrac{\\sqrt[3]{x}}{6x^3}\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\left(\\frac65x^{-7/2}-\\frac16x^{-8/3}\\right)\\,dx=-\\frac{12}{25}x^{-5/2}+\\frac1{10}x^{-5/3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>Find  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac{3\\sqrt{x}}{4x^4}-\\dfrac{x\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\right)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\left(\\frac34x^{-7/2}-x^{7/6}\\right)\\,dx=-\\frac3{10}x^{-5/2}-\\frac6{13}x^{13/6}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q22","number":22,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(x)=\\left(3x-\\dfrac4x\\right)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(2)=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=ax^3+bx+\\dfrac cx+d\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b,c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=9x^2-24+16x^{-2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=3x^3-24x-16x^{-1}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(2)=-2:-2=24-48-8+c\\Rightarrow c=30\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=3x^3-24x-\\frac{16}x+30\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q23","number":23,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given the gradient function is:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=kx^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=(kx)^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac1{kx^4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{18}{(2kx)^5}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac15kx^5+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac15k^4x^5+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac1kx^{-4}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac1{3k}x^{-3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac9{16k^5}x^{-5}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac9{64k^5}x^{-4}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q24","number":24,"question":"<p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{5+x^3}{x^2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{3x-2x^3}{x^5}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{8x^2-9}{x^4}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{30x^3-7}{14x^5}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(5x^{-2}+x)\\,dx=-5x^{-1}+\\frac12x^2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(3x^{-4}-2x^{-2})\\,dx=-x^{-3}+2x^{-1}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(8x^{-2}-9x^{-4})\\,dx=-8x^{-1}+3x^{-3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\left(\\frac{15}7x^{-2}-\\frac12x^{-5}\\right)\\,dx=-\\frac{15}7x^{-1}+\\frac18x^{-4}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q25","number":25,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given the gradient function is:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{5x^4-7}{5x^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{3-8x^3}{4x^5}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{6x^7-8}{12x^4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{8x-3x^2-6}{24x^5}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x-\\frac75x^{-3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac12x^2+\\frac7{10}x^{-2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac34x^{-5}-2x^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac3{16}x^{-4}+2x^{-1}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac12x^3-\\frac23x^{-4}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac18x^4+\\frac29x^{-3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac13x^{-4}-\\frac18x^{-3}-\\frac14x^{-5}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac19x^{-3}+\\frac1{16}x^{-2}+\\frac1{16}x^{-4}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q26","number":26,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(x)=\\dfrac{x-8}{x^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{ax^2+bx+c}{x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=x^{-2}-8x^{-3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=-x^{-1}+4x^{-2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(1)=0:0=-1+4+c\\Rightarrow c=-3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=-x^{-1}+4x^{-2}-3\\Rightarrow f(x)=-3-\\frac1x+\\frac4{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow f(x)=\\frac{-3x^2-x+4}{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q27","number":27,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(x)=\\left(\\dfrac{14-7x}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\right)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(1)=462\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=21x^{1/3}(ax^2+bx+c)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=\\frac{196-196x+49x^2}{x^{2/3}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow f'(x)=196x^{-2/3}-196x^{1/3}+49x^{4/3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=588x^{1/3}-147x^{4/3}+21x^{7/3}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(1)=462:462=588-147+21+c\\Rightarrow c=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=588x^{1/3}-147x^{4/3}+21x^{7/3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=21x^{1/3}(x^2-7x+28)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q28","number":28,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q28: Stationary Points</strong></p><p>A curve has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=3x^2+kx-21\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The curve has two turning points. One of the turning points is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the coordinates of the other turning point.</p>","steps":["<p>At the turning point, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=3+k-21\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=18\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2+18x-21=0\\text{ gives }x=1,\\ x=-7.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^3+9x^2-21x+c.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-6=1+9-21+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^3+9x^2-21x+5.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-7\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=250\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-7,250)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q29","number":29,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q29--Q30: The Factor Theorem</strong></p><p>A curve has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(x)=kx^2+74x+11\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(-1)=-100\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is also given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x+5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in its simplest form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\frac13kx^3+37x^2+11x+c.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-100)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-126=-\\frac13k+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-5,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-870=-\\frac{125}3k+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=18\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=-120\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=6x^3+37x^2+11x-120.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q30","number":30,"question":"<p>A curve has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(x)=576x^3+ax^2-208x+40\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6x-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are factors of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in its simplest form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=144x^4+\\frac13ax^3-104x^2+40x+c.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f\\left(\\frac65\\right)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{275}9=\\frac{125}{648}a+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f\\left(-\\frac12\\right)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"37=-\\frac1{24}a+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=-288\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=25\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=144x^4-96x^3-104x^2+40x+25.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q31","number":31,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q31: Binomial Expansion</strong></p><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int [(5+x)^4-(5-x)^4]\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int [(3+2x)^5-(3-2x)^5]\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int [(1-3x)^6-(1+3x)^6]\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int [(1+2x)^7-(1-2x)^7]\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(5+x)^4=x^4+20x^3+150x^2+500x+625\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(5-x)^4=x^4-20x^3+150x^2-500x+625\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(5+x)^4-(5-x)^4=40x^3+1000x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(40x^3+1000x)\\,dx=10x^4+500x^2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3+2x)^5=32x^5+240x^4+720x^3+1080x^2+810x+243\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3-2x)^5=-32x^5+240x^4-720x^3+1080x^2-810x+243\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3+2x)^5-(3-2x)^5=64x^5+1440x^3+1620x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(64x^5+1440x^3+1620x)\\,dx=\\frac{32}3x^6+360x^4+810x^2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-3x)^6=729x^6-1458x^5+1215x^4-540x^3+135x^2-18x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+3x)^6=729x^6+1458x^5+1215x^4+540x^3+135x^2+18x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-3x)^6-(1+3x)^6=-2916x^5-1080x^3-36x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(-2916x^5-1080x^3-36x)\\,dx=-486x^6-270x^4-18x^2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+2x)^7=128x^7+448x^6+672x^5+560x^4+280x^3+84x^2+14x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-2x)^7=-128x^7+448x^6-672x^5+560x^4-280x^3+84x^2-14x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+2x)^7-(1-2x)^7=256x^7+1344x^5+560x^3+28x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int(256x^7+1344x^5+560x^3+28x)\\,dx=32x^8+224x^6+140x^4+14x^2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q32","number":32,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has gradient function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=(4+2x)^3-(4-2x)^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,1024)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4(x^2+a)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an integer.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(4+2x)^3=8x^3+48x^2+96x+64\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(4-2x)^3=-8x^3+48x^2-96x+64\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(4+2x)^3-(4-2x)^3=16x^3+192x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=16x^3+192x\\Rightarrow y=4x^4+96x^2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(-2,1024):1024=64+384+c\\Rightarrow c=576\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=4x^4+96x^2+576\\Rightarrow y=4(x^4+24x^2+144)\\Rightarrow y=4(x^2+12)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q33","number":33,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q33: Second Derivatives</strong></p><p>Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=4x-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=6x^2-8x+9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=8x^3-7x^5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x+c_1,\\qquad y=\\frac32x^2+c_1x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x^2-5x+c_1,\\qquad y=\\frac23x^3-\\frac52x^2+c_1x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x^3-4x^2+9x+c_1,\\qquad y=\\frac12x^4-\\frac43x^3+\\frac92x^2+c_1x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x^4-\\frac76x^6+c_1,\\qquad y=\\frac25x^5-\\frac16x^7+c_1x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q34","number":34,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=\\sqrt{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=\\dfrac5{\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=\\dfrac3{x^3}-\\dfrac{x^3}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=\\dfrac8{x^4\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=x^{1/2}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac23x^{3/2}+c_1\\Rightarrow y=\\frac4{15}x^{5/2}+c_1x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=5x^{-1/2}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=10x^{1/2}+c_1\\Rightarrow y=\\frac{20}3x^{3/2}+c_1x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=3x^{-3}-\\frac13x^3\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac32x^{-2}-\\frac1{12}x^4+c_1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\frac32x^{-1}-\\frac1{60}x^5+c_1x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=8x^{-9/2}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{16}7x^{-7/2}+c_1\\Rightarrow y=\\frac{32}{35}x^{-5/2}+c_1x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q35","number":35,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^3y}{dx^3}=\\dfrac{10}{x\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^3y}{dx^3}=10x^{-3/2}\\Rightarrow\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=-20x^{-1/2}+c_1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-40x^{1/2}+c_1x+c_2\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac{80}3x^{3/2}+\\frac12c_1x^2+c_2x+c_3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q36","number":36,"question":"<p>It is given that the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(-3)=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(3)=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is also given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f''(x)=14-6x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in its simplest form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=14x-3x^2+c_1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(3)=2:2=42-27+c_1\\Rightarrow c_1=-13\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=14x-3x^2-13\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=7x^2-x^3-13x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(-3)=2:2=63+27+39+c_2\\Rightarrow c_2=-127\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=7x^2-x^3-13x-127\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q37","number":37,"question":"<p>It is given that the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(1)=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(1)=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is also given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f''(x)=36x^2+24x+12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in its simplest form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=12x^3+12x^2+12x+c_1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(1)=5:5=12+12+12+c_1\\Rightarrow c_1=-31\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=12x^3+12x^2+12x-31\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=3x^4+4x^3+6x^2-31x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(1)=3:3=3+4+6-31+c_2\\Rightarrow c_2=21\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=3x^4+4x^3+6x^2-31x+21\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q38","number":38,"question":"<p>It is given that the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(2)=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(1)=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is also given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f''(x)=\\dfrac{18}{x^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in its simplest form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f''(x)=18x^{-3},\\quad f'(x)=-9x^{-2}+c_1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(1)=-2:-2=-9+c_1\\Rightarrow c_1=7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=-9x^{-2}+7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=9x^{-1}+7x+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(2)=5:5=\\frac92+14+c_2\\Rightarrow c_2=-\\frac{27}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=9x^{-1}+7x-\\frac{27}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q39","number":39,"question":"<p>It is given that the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(1)=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(0)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is also given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f''(x)=210(x-\\sqrt{x}+x\\sqrt{x})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in its simplest form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f''(x)=210x-210x^{1/2}+210x^{3/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=105x^2-140x^{3/2}+84x^{5/2}+c_1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(0)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=0-0+0+c_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c_1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=105x^2-140x^{3/2}+84x^{5/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=35x^3-56x^{5/2}+24x^{7/2}+c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(1)=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"11=35-56+24+c_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c_2=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=35x^3-56x^{5/2}+24x^{7/2}+8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.36-q40","number":40,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q40: Stationary Points</strong></p><p>It is given that the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(2)=-37\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(1)=-15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is also given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f''(x)=12(kx-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the curve has a stationary point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\dfrac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in its simplest form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f''(x)=12kx-12,\\qquad f'(x)=6kx^2-12x+c_1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(1)=-15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-15=6k-12+c_1\\Rightarrow-3=6k+c_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'\\left(\\frac12\\right)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=\\frac32k-6+c_1\\Rightarrow6=\\frac32k+c_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c_1=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=-12x^2-12x+9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=-4x^3-6x^2+9x+c_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(2)=-37\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-37=-32-24+18+c_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c_2=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=-4x^3-6x^2+9x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]